message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Spark IIS API: fail-closed Integration-Interaction-Stimulation reference server"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
version: "0.1.0"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/spark-iis-api"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  Fail-closed reference server (FastAPI, Pydantic v2) for an accessible
  integration, interaction and stimulation API with simulated display, audio,
  haptic and sensor devices only. A locked safety envelope refuses flicker
  above 3 Hz (WCAG 2.3.1), saturated-red flashes, flashing fields over 25%,
  audio above 70 dB(A), long continuous vibration and sessions over 20 min;
  unknown fields are refused; stop always succeeds; sensors can only dim or
  stop; and a residual latch (S = 0.45 Peak + 0.35 RMS + 0.20 MeanAbs >= 0.50
  on 32-value blocks) stops output on bad or missing data. Sessions are
  archived with a provenance manifest and evidence report. Not a medical
  device; no therapeutic, neurological, coherence, HBOT-synergy or quantum
  effect is claimed or established.
keywords:
  - accessibility
  - assistive-technology
  - safety-envelope
  - fail-closed
  - photosensitivity
  - wcag
  - fastapi
  - simulation
  - provenance
  - research-software
